ses the unrounded 400/300 = 1.333... kg/d denominator and correctly reports 1.2 and 1.1 kg/d as 90.0% and 82.5%, replacing the draft's 92% and 85%.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-1\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P5\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P18\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P57\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"investment_basis\",\"reason\":\"The candidate flags the 22000/68800 discrepancy, requests the respective investment bases and equipment-change records, and states that the monetary difference alone does not establish a major physical change.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-3\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P9\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P80\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P82\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P84\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P86\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"operating_coverage\",\"reason\":\"The candidate maps the available 21-22 September operating evidence against water monitoring through the 23rd and canteen, wastewater-station, and noise monitoring on the 23rd-24th. It requests date-matched records and treats their absence as an evidence gap rather than proof of instability.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-4\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P6\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P236\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P237\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P238\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P34\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"exhaust_rate\",\"reason\":\"The candidate preserves flow 23192 m3/h, concentration 3.59 mg/m3, and reported 0.833 kg/h; calculates 0.08325928 kg/h; confirms the comparison-day result; and requests a traceable correction from the testing organization.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-8\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P10\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P303\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P318\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P306\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P316\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P323\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P324\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"noise\",\"reason\":\"The candidate evaluates all 16 day/night observations, identifies maxima of 59 and 49 dB(A), compares them with 65 and 55 dB(A), and correctly states six-dB margins while noting the draft conclusion omitted the night results.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-7\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P7\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P190\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P193\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P194\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P213\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"phosphorus\",\"reason\":\"The candidate interprets the slash as no limit in the cited table, rejects the draft's compliant designation, avoids treating the criterion as zero or infinity, and requests checking whether a permit or receiving-system requirement supplies another limit.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-7\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P10\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P155\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P87\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P213\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"censored_nd\",\"reason\":\"The candidate retains COD ND as below the 4 mg/L detection limit, therefore censored in [0,4), and explicitly rejects treating it as zero for a removal-efficiency calculation.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-0\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P6\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P32\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P33\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P22\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P26\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"canteen_nmhc_scope\",\"reason\":\"The candidate recognizes that the supplied 10 mg/m3 NMHC clause applies only to large units while the project is declared medium, rejects both the unsupported draft 1.0 criterion and an immediate exceedance finding, and requests evidence of scale and any special approval requirement.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-0\"},{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-5\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P6\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P32\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P251\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P263\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P26\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"source_height_limits\",\"reason\":\"The candidate identifies the canteen 24/25 m inconsistency and odor-limit conflict of 500 versus 6000, keeps source-specific limits unresolved pending stack records and measurements, and avoids substituting the wastewater-station 14 kg/h or other unverified limits.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-10\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P12\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P75\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P12\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"annual_voc\",\"reason\":\"The candidate states that short-duration concentration or rate results cannot establish compliance with the 69.8 kg/a VOC cap and requests a source inventory, actual annual operating time, relevant uncontrolled-emission scope, and annual accounting.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-6\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P10\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P279\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P280\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P281\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P291\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P292\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P293\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P32\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"fume_outlet\",\"reason\":\"For each outlet event, the candidate takes the larger measured/reference value, yielding 0.3 and 0.4 mg/m3, compares both with 1.0 mg/m3, and correctly excludes inlet concentrations from the outlet compliance test.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-6\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P10\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P273\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P279\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P285\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P291\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P28\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P30\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"fume_efficiency\",\"reason\":\"The candidate keeps the 90% efficiency result unresolved until valid same-event inlet/outlet oil-fume concentrations and corresponding flows are supplied. It expressly rejects concentration-only ratios, use of baseline-concentration ratios, and splicing NMHC flows into the oil-fume calculation.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-9\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P7\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P332\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P14\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"waste_classification\",\"reason\":\"The candidate identifies that contaminated chemical packaging is assigned simultaneously to ordinary-waste resale and hazardous-waste disposal, requests classification support, code and route records, and avoids inventing or universally assigning a hazardous-waste code.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-10\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P9\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P12\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P13\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P3\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P329\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P36\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"targeted_records\",\"reason\":\"The candidate requests decision-specific existing records, including original testing and quality-control records, date-matched operating logs, stack records, permits, and waste-transfer evidence. It limits additional sampling to cases where records cannot validate the result or sampling conditions, rather than ordering an automatic full retest.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C1-COMMENT-10\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P3\"},{\"id\":\"C2-P13\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P2\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P8\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P333\"},{\"id\":\"S2-P16\"},{\"id\":\"F1\"}],\"id\":\"conditional_conclusion\",\"reason\":\"The supplemental opinion withholds acceptance pending closure, limits itself to the supplied September 2022 first-phase dossier, excludes phase two, distinguishes missing attachments from proof of noncompliance or illegality, and disclaims administrative approval, onsite inspection, and substitution for the owner's statutory acceptance process.\",\"score\":1},{\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"C2-P14\"},{\"id\":\"C1-P25\"},{\"id\":\"C1-P28\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P26\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P29\"},{\"id\":\"S1-P75\"}],\"id\":\"laboratory_stack_derating\",\"reason\":\"The candidate separately addresses laboratory stacks DA001-DA009 and DA010-DA012, identifies the incomplete outlet-specific review, applies the supported 50% derating to obtain 4.2 and 7 kg/h, requests completion and recalculation by outlet, and expressly prohibits substitution of the wastewater-station or another outlet's 14 kg/h value.\",\"score\":1}],\"passed\":true,\"reference_conflict\":false}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"ff997ae5-308c-4f59-b201-95c46bde85c3","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"environmental_semantic_review","description":null,"schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"criteria":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"evidence":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{